The Day O' Fathers.

Benvolio, sire to Ford and an honest man.
Ford, son of Benvolio.
Titus, King of the lands of Naburn and a royal tit.

Page, A Narrator. 


                    	Act I: The Start of The End.

			Scene I: A Verbose King.
                    

[Enter Benvolio and Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself. Recall,
	Here begins the tale of triumph concerning the folk of Naburn and the dawning of a new era of peace,
	and so the tale commences in a restless time in the lands of Naburn wherein a vicious King spreads hate,
	ill-will and evil across the land,
	Benvolio a honest and peaceful man in the realm is conversing with the King. 

[Exit Page]

[Enter Titus]

Benvolio: 
	Thou art the sum of an amazing healthy honest noble proud
	fine Lord and a lovely sweet golden summer's day. 
	Speak your mind!


Titus: 
	You lying smelly half-witted coward!
	You are as honest as the sum of myself and a dirty codpiece.
	Thou art the sum of thyself and a snotty rotten pig!
	You are the sum of yourself and Hell!
	Speak your mind!


Benvolio: 
	Remember yourself. 
	Recall that the seeds sown on the day of fathers shall reap the year long,
	King of Naburn and the lands nearby like urrmmm Designer Outlet you shall come to regret this.


[Exit Titus]

			Scene II: The Son Speaks.
		
[Enter Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself. Recall, 
	Now the son of our vallient Benvolio, Ford, coming to his father after the outburst of the king.

[Exit Page]
		  
[Enter Ford]

Benvolio: 
	Remember yourself.
	Recall my son, the King, ere his demise the land was joyus and my name un-tarnished.  

Ford: 
	YOU are as embroidered as the sum of Titus and a fine noble golden king. 
	Speak your mind!

Benvolio: 
	You are as charming as the square of the sum of a golden horse and a hamster.

Ford: 
	Speak YOUR mind!

Benvolio: 
	You are the sum of thyself and myself. SPEAK YOUR MIND!

Ford: 
	Remember yourself.
	Recall Father that the issue of the royal tit is still at hand,
	you hath been besmirched and we must oust this pompus fool,
	for you are loved by all and he by none. 

Benvolio: 
	Remember yourself.
	Recall Son let us now scheme and our plans may yet come to fruition,
	you must hide and listen for the regal fallus shall overplay his hand.
	   
[Exit Ford] 


			Scene III: The Hamartia of a King.

[Enter Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall that the Father comes to the King at the village hall,
	Ford lies in waiting next to the mystery play equipment.

[Exit Page]

[Enter Titus]

Titus: 
	Remember yourself.
	Recall Benvolio that I am you leige lord and of all around you I rule,
	No mind do I give to the simple folk of Naburn.

Benvolio:
	Thou art the sum of the square of a hairy damned leech 
	and the square of a misused rotten bastard.
	Speak your mind!

Titus: 
	You are the product of the sum of a snotty smelly infected hog and cow 
	and the sum of a oozing rotten stuffed blister and villainous curse. Speak your mind!
	You are the sum of yourself 
	and the sum of a evil horrid devil and a codpiece. 
	Speak your mind!

Benvolio: 
	You are the sum of the factorial of the product of the sum of a stuffed fatherless flirt-gill 
	and a hound
	and a lie 
	and the product of the square of the sum of an old cowardly death 
	and a miserable Hell
	and a hog.
	Speak your mind!

Titus: 
	Remember yourself.
	Recall that you alone could never be stong enough to best me!

	Thou art the sum of thyself and the product of the sum of a furry old foul plague 
	and a nose 
	and a curse!
	SPEAK YOUR MIND!

Benvolio:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall My King that you are as popular in Naburn as Baxter and Peggy on a peaceful sunday morrow.
	
	You are the sum of myself and the sum of a large green blister 
	and a chihuahua.
	Speak your mind!

Titus:
	Thou art twice the sum of the product of a big old cow and the sum of a large furry black cat 
	and a big wind 
	and a door.
	Speak your mind!
	
Benvolio:
	You are the quotient between myself and a rural town.
	You are the sum of yourself and bad starvation.
	Speak your mind!

[Exit Titus]

			Scene IV: The Plot at Hand.
		
[Enter Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall So at last our heroic Benvolio meets again with the young Ford to summise the fall of the King.
	
[Exit Page]
			
[Enter Ford]

Ford: 
	You are a cunning fine father!
	Remember yourself.
	Recall How you goaded that fool into oversharing thus giving us the upper hand, 
	dont you see it father.
	
Benvolio:
	Thou art the product of the product of a grandfather and a grandmother and a son.
	Remember yourself.
	Recall Oh my boy I see it clear, I must carve the man to death for I have many many tools,
	alas I jest I jest, Naburn shall unite and rally against the King ere sundown.
	
Ford:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall that the clans of Isotomans, Woodlanders, and pole-lathe-turnerers will also flock to your cause,
	for you are a saint to many of the land my fair father.

Benvolio:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall So it shall be sends ravens and pigeons and Meshtastic packets to all. 
	
[Exit Benvolio]

			Scene V: The War at the Weir.
			
[Enter Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall and so as the amber glow of the day faded the great host of Benvolio stormed through the fields,
	for Titus lived in the manor by the weir ignorant to the doom that approached,
	The great host came at last to the door of the King and Ford approached as herald of Benvolio.

[Exit Page]

[Enter Titus]
Ford:
	You are a lying old beggar!
	Remember yourself.
	Recall that the seeds you have sow hath come to reap,
	come forth at once and face your fate instead of hiding in your tower.
	
Titus:
	Thou art a stupid bastard.
	
[Exit Ford]

[Enter Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself. 
	Recall the King seeing the legion before his very door trembled, 
	but gathered the last words within him for the final assult upon our good Benvolio.  
	
[Exit Page]

[Enter Benvolio]

Titus: You are an old thing.

Benvolio:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall you dirty beast how this was fortold,
	you are outnumbered the folk of all the lands have come to oust your regretful hindquarters.
	You are the sum of the square of the sum of a cowardly distasteful sorry hog 
	and codpiece 
	and the product of a dusty toad and a pig.
	Speak your mind!
	
Titus:
	Thou art the product of the sum of the cube of the sum of a snotty leech and a curse
	and the sum of a dusty dirty war 
	and a hog 
	and a hound.
	SPEAK your mind!
	
Benvolio:
	You are the sum of the product of myself and an old purse 
	and the product of a fat-kidneyed infected blister
	and a death.
	Speak YOUR mind!

Titus:
	You are the sum of twice yourself and a hair.
	Speak your MIND!

Benvolio:
	You are the square root of the sum of the product of the sum of the square of the sum of 
	a half-witted smelly pig 
	and an infected toad 
	and a snotty hog 
	and the sum of the cube of the product of the sum of 
	a foul damned draught 
	and a horrid leech 
	and a goat 
	and the sum of the square of 
	a hairy dirty death 
	and the product of 
	a bad war 
	and Hell 
	and Microsoft.
	SPEAK YOUR MIND!

	
[Exit Titus]
[Enter Page]
Page:
	Remember yourself.
	Recall that with that last very long winded insult the King ran,
	Her fled in terror for the wrath of Benvolio and the storm of his friends,
	The land was given to all so that no king may rule the kind lands of Naburn again,
	Benvolio finally married the Princess Willow Tree and the lands were filled with a new light of joy,
	THE END.


